WEBVTT

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:14.040
What's wrong, Aries?

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.910
This is strange.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:19.200
I don't remember you, Charce.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:25.410
I went to biology class many times after
I transferred in, before leaving for camp.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:29.450
I have no doubt that Charce
was not in that class.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:32.410
Charce, are you...

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:34.040
Are you hiding something?

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.000
What does this mean?

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.330
Charce, please explain.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:49.540
So you trust Aries over me? That's sad.

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:56.160
I'm a transfer student.

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:00.750
I entered Caird High after Aries.

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.370
Right before camp.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.660
What?!

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:07.540
Charce is a transfer student, too? Like Aries?

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.870
And right before camp...?

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:12.370
I transferred in on July 1st.

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:16.500
There was no biology class before July 4th.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.450
Why didn't you tell us?!

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:22.700
I didn't think it was relevant.
Is this all that important?

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:26.080
But... when Aries brought up the fact
that she's a transfer student,

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:29.750
wouldn't the natural reaction be
to talk about yourself? It's weird!

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.200
We all like you, Charce.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:36.700
Without your achievements,
we wouldn't have made it this far.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.620
We're all very grateful.

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:45.040
But one thing that bothers me is that
you almost never talk about yourself.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:48.660
Don't you see us as your friends?

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:52.660
It's not up to us to decide how much
personal information he wants to discuss.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:56.120
I'm sure there are things he doesn't want
to talk about, like any of us.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:58.910
But we're not under normal circumstances.

00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:01.580
Saying you transferred in right before camp

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:04.950
is almost like admitting you're
the enemy sent in to kill us.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:08.620
Charce, explain why you didn't tell us.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:10.290
If I refuse?

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:11.870
I'd have to lock you up.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:19.000
Okay, fine. Solid performance, Captain.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:23.790
I didn't mention the transfer because
I didn't want to talk about my family.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:28.790
I could have made up a more plausible story,
but I didn't want to lie to you.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:30.540
Because you all are my friends.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:37.410
I'm from a noble family
in the Vixia Royal Quarter.

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:39.080
Vixia Royal Quarter?!

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:40.290
Seriously?!

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:43.410
I've never heard of that, what's Vixia?

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:47.750
It's the only part of the world
where there are kings and nobles.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:52.700
I didn't talk about this because
I was told not to discuss it...

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:56.410
And also because I wanted to forget about it.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:04.870
After the end of the world war, a global
government was established in 1963 A.D.

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:09.950
All nations were reorganized,
and Vixia was the only one that was allowed

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:11.870
to maintain rule by royalty.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:18.410
Life there is idyllic.
Science and technology are restricted,

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:21.700
maintaining a sort of pretend-Medieval era.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:27.120
It has a fairy tale feel to it,
so it's a popular tourist destination.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.910
But the central area, surrounded by walls,

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:34.750
is off limits to tourists and ordinary citizens.

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:37.660
It's where the royalty and nobles live.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:40.790
I was born into a noble family.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:47.410
Phew, I made it out!

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:48.910
Come here, Seira.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:55.290
You're right! No alarms!

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.120
I found a crack and opened it up a little.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:03.580
They'll find it and fix it soon,
but we can play in the noble area today!

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:09.750
But this noble's outfit won't fool them--
they'll know I'm a commoner.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:14.950
Don't worry! You look great!
Just like I imagined!

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:18.870
Thanks, Charce...
But you're being kind of creepy.

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:25.330
Seira is a commoner, but we got along well,
so we hung out a lot.

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:28.700
Of course, normally we met
in the commoner area.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:33.200
But that day, I took a risk
and invited her into the nobles' area.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:36.330
There was a place I wanted to take her.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.910
The royal zoo?

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.790
You said you wanted to visit there, right?

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:42.750
There are lots of unique animals there!

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.080
I want to go!

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:45.500
Let's go then!

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.750
Come on, hurry, hurry!

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:50.910
Careful, watch where you're going!

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:52.080
I'm sorry.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:53.950
Wait!

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:58.660
This girl is a commoner.
How are you here without a permit?

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:00.200
I let her in!

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:01.410
How did you get in?!

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:02.290
Let go of me!

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:03.450
Are you a trespasser?

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:04.700
Please, wait!

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:06.080
Come here!

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:09.290
Dirty commoner!

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.290
Seira!

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.370
Seira!

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:20.500
--Someone fell!
--Hey, look!

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:21.830
Call a doctor!

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:28.370
Are you going to see that commoner girl again?

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:30.000
Know your place! You're a noble!

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.910
Nobles are just caged animals!

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:34.660
I'm going to live free!

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.160
Seira...

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:40.700
You've been asleep for a while now.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:43.120
I'll visit you every day.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:46.700
I'll study biology and teach you all about it.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:50.080
When you wake up, we can go
to the forest with the squirrels.

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:52.080
Take your time.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.910
Rest now, Seira...

00:05:56.250 --> 00:06:02.450
Four years later, Seira's family left Vixia
without telling me where they went.

00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:06.750
Seira is probably still quietly sleeping,
somewhere in the world.

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:11.000
A while later, I left Vixia as well.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.370
"Lacroix" is my adopted mother's last name.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:15.450
I'm sorry I kept this from you.

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:19.750
I lost a close friend
and cut ties with my family.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:24.370
I was just getting started with a new life,
and my head wasn't clear yet.

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:26.790
That's why I never got around
to discussing any of this.

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:28.290
I'm truly sorry.

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:29.540
Seira...

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:30.660
"Gloom"

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:31.580
"Gloom"
What?!

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:32.450
"Gloom"

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:35.370
What... What's wrong, everyone?!

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:39.450
I'm sorry, Charce...
It must still be very difficult for you.

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:42.250
It was insensitive of me.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:48.500
No, I should have told you sooner.
I didn't think this would interest you.

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:52.660
But do you have to cry so much?
It's about someone you don't even know.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:54.040
Idiot!

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:57.120
It's about someone dear to you!

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.200
It doesn't matter if we know her or not!

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:07.700
Hey, what are you laughing about?!

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:10.660
Don't be mad. I laughed because you all cried.

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:13.080
We're crying because we're sad!

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:15.370
And I'm glad you're crying.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.370
So, we're crying because we're sad,

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.620
you're laughing because you're glad,
which made him mad.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:22.040
--I left everything behind.
--Thanks for the confusing summary.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.410
But why...

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:26.830
Another family...

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:30.700
I'll make more mushroom tea.

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:31.910
Oh, for me too please.

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:33.330
Thanks!

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:35.830
I'll help.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:41.290
Seira must be very dear to you.

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:43.870
What is she like?

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:46.200
She's like you, Aries.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.700
What?

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:51.500
Team B5, camp log.

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:56.790
With many different thoughts on our minds,
we approach the next planet.

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:08.660
I'm sorry, Seira.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:16.910
"Planet Icriss
Day 75 of being lost in space"

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:19.370
Here we are, number four!

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:22.700
--♪ Turning, turning, the planet is turning! ♪
--We had a few bumps, but overall
this has been a good trip.

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:26.750
--♪ Turning, turning, the planet is turning! ♪
--I'm starting to get used to it.

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:29.830
--♪ It turns with our hopes on board! ♪

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:31.910
--What are they doing?
--♪ It turns with our hopes on board! ♪

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:36.450
--Caird High, choir competition set piece,
"The Planet Turns."
--♪ It turns with our hopes on board! ♪

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:38.830
No, this one isn't turning.

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:40.080
What?!

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:44.250
To be precise, this planet's rotation
and orbital revolution are in sync.

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:47.160
So the sun never sets there?

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:49.410
Great, sunshine!

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:53.080
That's kind of exciting, isn't it? Yeah!

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:54.080
Idiots!

00:08:55.120 --> 00:09:01.040
It's a burning death zone!
No water, and definitely no life!

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.830
What?! Who just said "Yeah!"?

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:05.540
You did!

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:07.080
So the other side is...

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:10.540
Frozen, dark, death zone.

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:15.830
Oh Zack, please tell us there's a place
to find liquid water and life?

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:18.580
According to the data on the planet list, yes.

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:22.790
This would be where to look.
The belt separating the two death zones.

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:26.450
Good, we know where to land. Let's go!

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:38.000
So this is Planet Icriss.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:41.950
Are those trees?
They're the size of skyscrapers.

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:46.500
What are these, birds?!

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:48.290
So huge...

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:54.000
They're not attacking us. They also seem
lighter weight relative to their size.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:59.580
Seems close to insects. We should be okay
as long as we're on the ship.

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:01.450
Oh, balloons.

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:02.620
What?

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:07.910
What?!

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:11.500
What is this, electricity?
It's dropping the insects that touch it!

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:15.120
Zack! Sparkles! Dodge! Don't touch!

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:18.160
I know! If you're going to give commands,
keep it together!

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:22.330
Did we... make it through?

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:24.370
What was all that about?!

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:27.870
Probably a type of carnivorous plant.

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:32.200
It seems like this region has many plants
that ensnare and eat flying creatures.

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:34.950
Let's land quickly then, Kanata!

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:38.250
No, not yet. This area isn't safe.

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:43.450
If we get out of the sunlight a bit more,
we shouldn't see any more of those plants.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:45.200
Head towards the cold area!

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:46.410
Aye, yeah.

00:10:56.910 --> 00:10:58.500
What is this?!

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:00.370
It's breaking the ship apart!

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:02.120
Shake it off, Zack!

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:08.450
This thing is too strong!

00:11:08.450 --> 00:11:12.290
It's a mass of muscle! Is it really a plant?!

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:14.540
Hold on! I'm making it spin!

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:30.620
Yes!

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:31.910
We made it out!

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:37.830
What's wrong?!

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:39.790
Error reported in the control system!

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:42.450
I'm losing attitude and deceleration controls!

00:11:42.450 --> 00:11:43.370
What?!

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:44.830
Watch the cliffs!

00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:47.620
I don't have portside controls! I can't turn left!

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:51.620
Why is this happening all at once?!
Too many things!

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:57.040
Things were too easy until now!
This must be what space adventure is really like.

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:02.620
I'm counting on you, Zack...

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:04.910
This is our only ship.

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:07.790
If it breaks, we're done for...

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:11.000
I've got this. I can do it...

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.290
Almost there...

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:17.160
A gust?!

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:58.750
The <i>Astra</i>...

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.580
...has lost navigation.

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:15.450
I took a look at the damaged parts.

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:20.080
The bridge and the aft engines are fine.
It can fly a little.

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:21.950
A little...?

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:25.330
We can't go to space. We can't fix it either.

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:29.950
The fore reactors are completely broken.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:32.700
We can't generate energy
for super high-speed travel.

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:35.080
We have no parts, no tools, no dock.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:40.500
We can slowly move the ship across
the surface, but not get to space.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:43.580
What's going to happen to us...?

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:47.950
Our trip ends here.
We have to live on this planet.

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:49.370
You've got to be kidding me!

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:52.000
How are we supposed to live on this planet?!

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:56.370
Only the front part is damaged.
The residential area is fine.

00:13:56.370 --> 00:13:58.040
We can live on the ship.

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:02.950
That's not what I'm talking about.
I want to go home, to my actual home!

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:06.750
That's just not possible.
Do I need to repeat the explanation?

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:10.870
Please say you're lying...

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:24.870
So it's really over? No more going home?

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:27.000
Why did this happen?!

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:34.910
It's my fault. If I paid more attention
when flying the ship...

00:14:34.910 --> 00:14:40.330
No, you did well. The responsibility
is mine, as the commander.

00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:46.290
I thought we could get home if we
worked together, one step at a time...

00:14:48.540 --> 00:14:51.620
You're out of character, boss man.

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:54.950
I thought you're supposed to act tough
when things look bad.

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:58.410
Isn't there something
in your survival tips thing?

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:02.290
Like, "If you stand still you don't move
forward" or something?

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:04.080
Ulgar...

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:10.450
Yeah. You're right. I'm sorry.

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:13.250
Wherever we're going to live, we need to eat.

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:17.080
We're running out of food.
Let's go and explore this place.

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:20.620
Survival tip number 10: if you stand still
you don't move forward!

00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:22.540
You totally made that up right now!

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:28.330
Thanks, Ulgar.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:33.870
It's starting to snow!

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:35.540
We're close to the boundary between
the belt area and the frozen area.

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:38.540
"Food search party
Charce, Ulgar, Luca, Yunhua, Funicia"
We're close to the boundary between
the belt area and the frozen area.

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:43.120
We can see the sun, but we'll still freeze
if we don't wear our suits.

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:46.040
I see berries. Are those edible?

00:15:47.700 --> 00:15:48.790
Yummy.

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:49.660
It's edible.

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:53.500
Ulgar, you're impressive.
It's nice watching you work.

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:57.910
I see a few berries, but no animals around.

00:15:57.910 --> 00:16:00.540
Can we catch those big bugs?

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:03.160
That might be hard.

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:05.660
We'd need nets the size of soccer goals.

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:10.080
So... everyone's accepted it now?

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:13.790
You have nerves of steel. I can't do that.

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:16.500
They're just trying to keep up appearances.

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:22.200
We'll get swallowed up by despair if we don't
do anything, so we do what we can.

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:25.040
Nobody can accept hopelessness so quickly.

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:31.000
Ulgar, I didn't realize you're scared too.

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:33.910
Who would've thought with that
"I'm ready for anything" look.

00:16:33.910 --> 00:16:35.450
I'm not scared!

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:43.200
Hey, Charce, let's go look over
there too--behind the cliff.

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:44.540
Behind the cliff?

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:47.750
There won't be any plants
where the sun isn't shining.

00:16:47.750 --> 00:16:50.200
Oh, right. But over there...

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:51.540
I see something.

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:52.660
Hmm?

00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:57.750
What is that...?

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:08.750
"Water search party
Kanata, Aries, Zack, Quitterie"
Good, there's no problem with the water.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:11.200
Yeah, I'm glad we were able to move the ship.

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:15.250
Quitterie, you need to switch gears.

00:17:15.250 --> 00:17:17.620
We have to think about surviving.

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:20.620
What's the point of surviving here?!

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:23.080
There were so many things I wanted to do.

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:27.750
Eat good food, dress well.
I had a vision of the future, too.

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:31.370
Go to college, become a doctor, get married...

00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:33.370
But now...

00:17:33.370 --> 00:17:36.330
...I'm stuck to die in this unknown place!

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:38.450
How can you be so calm?!

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:41.750
My job is to stay calm.

00:17:41.750 --> 00:17:46.370
I cool down when others are panicking.

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:49.330
Quitterie, you have to decide
to live here with the others

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:52.410
or place your bets on
a low probability, alone.

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:54.410
Low probability?

00:17:54.410 --> 00:18:00.290
Did you know? The <i>Astra </i>has just one
functioning hibernation device.

00:18:00.290 --> 00:18:03.250
You can use that to wait for help...

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:04.870
Wait for help?

00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:09.540
How do you let people know
you're waiting for help here?

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:12.120
That's why I said "wait."

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:17.870
Betting on a low probability--
it might take decades, or centuries.

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:22.830
Long after the others die of old age,
you'd keep waiting, in your sleep.

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:27.790
Maybe nobody comes, but you bet on
the slim chance that someone will come

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:30.580
to explore this planet in the future.

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:35.290
Why... would you say that?

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:39.000
That's like telling me to die alone.

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:42.950
I'm sorry. That's the only way
I can think of to return home.

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:50.500
No! I don't want to be alone!
Are you an idiot?! Stop being so mean!

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:55.160
Let's live together. On this planet.
With the others.

00:18:56.330 --> 00:19:01.290
Kanata, you look ready. I'm impressed.

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:06.120
You're giving me too much credit.
I'm not ready, and I might not be until I die.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:08.080
I'll just have to move on however I can.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:13.330
That said, I'm not very sensitive.
I feel like I can survive anywhere.

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:17.000
I was also hoping we could make a stone axe
or something and fix this,

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:20.120
over like ten years or so.

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:28.000
I'll be okay with that, too.
As long as you're around.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:28.790
Huh?

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:30.580
I mean, so, um...

00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:32.330
Yeah, I get it.

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:33.950
What?!

00:19:33.950 --> 00:19:37.000
It's Charce. He wants us to come right away.

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:39.200
What happened?

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:41.290
Over there, by that cliff.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:52.120
What... is this?

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:54.330
What does this mean?

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:58.540
I have no idea... I have no idea at all.

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:03.080
Why is there...

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:08.040
...another <i>Astra </i>on this planet...?

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:15.330
No, it's much more weathered,
and the damaged parts are different.

00:20:15.330 --> 00:20:17.200
It's a different ship of the same type.

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:19.450
Let's go inside, a team of three.

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:23.500
Me, Zack, and...

00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:25.750
Ulgar, come with us.

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:26.950
Yeah.

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:39.000
Power is active.

00:20:40.870 --> 00:20:42.450
Going inside now.

00:20:46.790 --> 00:20:49.080
Same internal structure...

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:54.910
This ship is in bad shape.

00:20:54.910 --> 00:20:56.660
It's like a ruin.

00:20:57.700 --> 00:21:03.000
Ship broke down, stuck on this planet...
Just like us, it seems.

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:07.580
With this much damage on the bridge,
this ship is incapable of space flight.

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:08.830
I see...

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:12.000
I checked the residential area.
There's no one there.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:17.620
So maybe the crew was rescued
but the ship was left behind.

00:21:18.950 --> 00:21:22.330
No, there's a message left behind.

00:21:22.330 --> 00:21:24.250
"Help me"...

00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:27.700
Weren't they rescued?!
Why leave a message on the ship?

00:21:27.700 --> 00:21:31.000
Help... I get it!

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:32.700
It's the hibernation device!

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:40.450
The device is active.

00:21:40.450 --> 00:21:42.910
There's someone inside.

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:48.830
July 2051... 12 years ago.

00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:53.830
Twelve years... Waiting so long for help...

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:55.370
What should we do, Kanata?

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:58.200
Let's wake them.

00:22:14.160 --> 00:22:15.750
It's a woman...
